    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1295">

                <pb facs="1110" n="1006" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1006"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 412.11T54/205.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-01-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 30, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Minister for Foreign Affairs, after an interview with the President, said
                    to-day to Mr. Schuyler that he would soon send me a note refusing arbitration,
                    not only because arbitration is impracticable on the basis of the protocol, but
                    because the Government and the Company were expecting to arrange an amicable
                    settlement, the terms of which will be submitted to the Department which, he
                    said, had agreed to be judge of its justice.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
